 are pure pipes now these pipes  are pipes that use pure functions  as a result of this a pure pipe doesn't  use  any internal state and the output  remains the same as long as the  parameters  passed stay the same angular calls a  pure pipe  only when it detects a change in the  parameters being passed  now a single instance of a pure pipe is  used throughout all components  next up what are impure pipes  now for every change detection cycle in  angular  these impure pipes are called regardless  of the change in the input fields  as long as there's a change detected  these pipes are called  as a result multiple pipe instances are  created for these pipes  now inputs passed to these pipes can  also be mutable  by default all pipes are pure however  you can also  mention impure pipes using the pure  property  now here's a code for specifying impure  pipes  you can use the pure property and either  mention true or false  true meaning it's a pure pipe and false  indicates that it's an impure pipe  next up what is the pipe transform  interface  now as the name suggests the interface  receives an input value  and transforms it into the desired  format with a transform method  it is typically used to implement custom  pipes  now here's again a small piece of code  now you can see that the pipe transform  interface is being used  which in turn executes the transform  method now this transform method is the  one that is responsible to  change your input and give a transformed  output  moving on what is ng module  now ng modules are basically containers  that reserve a block of code to an  application domain  or a workflow now the at ng module  takes a metadata object that describes  how to compile a components template  and generate an injector at runtime in  addition to this  ng module also identifies the modules  components  detectives services pipes and also  ensures  that it makes them public so that  external components can use them  all of this is taken care of by the ng  module  next up what are filters in angular  now filters are used to format an  expression  and present it to the user they can be  used in  view templates controllers or services  now to name a few there's  date filter which formats a date to a  specified format  there's filter filter that selects a  subset of items from an array  there's the json filter which formats an  object  to a json string there's limit 2 which  limits an array or a string into a  specified number of elements or  characters  then there's lowercase which formats a  string to lowercase  and so on moving on to the next question  what is view encapsulation in angular  now view encapsulation basically defines  whether the template and styles defined  within the component  can affect the application or vice versa  angular provides three encapsulation  strategies  there's emulated encapsulation which  means that the styles from the main html  propagate to the component then there is  native  which indicates that the styles from the  main html do not propagated the  component  meaning it does not affect the component  and lastly there is none  which means that styles from the  component propagate back to the  main html and therefore are visible to  all the components on the page  now this indicates any different types  of changes and how it is affecting the  entire application  moving on what are controllers now  as the name suggests controllers control  the data of angular applications  they are regular javascript objects and  the ng controller directive defines the  application controller  next question what do you understand by  scope in angular  now the scope in angular binds the html  that is basically the view and the  javascript that is the controller  it is also an object with the available  properties and methods required for your  application  now when you make a controller in  angular you pass the dollar scope object  as an argument moving on to the most  commonly asked question  explain the life cycle hooks in angular  as discussed earlier every component in  angular has a life cycle  angular creates and renders these  components and also destroys them  before removing them from the document  object model  it is achieved with the help of these  life cycle hooks  now let's have a look at them first up  is ng on changes  now this responds when angular sets or  resets  data bound input properties  ng on it is a hook that initializes  the directive or a component after  angular first displays  the data bound properties and sets the  components  input properties ng do check  detects and acts upon the changes that  angular can't  or won't detect on its own  ng after content init responds after  ng projects external content into the  components view  ng after content checked response after  angular checks the content  projected into the component  ng after in it responds after angular  initializes  the components views and child views  ng after view checked responds after  angular checks the components views and  the child views  lastly there's ng on destroy which  cleans up  just before angular destroys the  directive or the component  moving on to the next question what is  string interpolation  in angular now string interpolation  is a one-way data binding technique that  is used by angular  now it outputs the data from typescript  code to html view  it is typically denoted with the help of  curly braces  and it helps display data from the  component to the view  to help you understand it's working i've  created a variable called name  here in my app.component.ts file  and initialize it to simplylon and back  in my html file  i've created a heading tag  a header tag which displays the name of  the company is  and i've interpolated here with the help  of double curly braces  so when i run the file the output looks  something like this  the name of the company is simply learn  so this is how string interpolation is  achieved  in angular moving on to next question  what are template statements  template statements are properties or  methods used in html  for responding to user events now with  these template statements  the application that you create or  you're working on  can have the capability to engage users  through actions such as submitting forms  or displaying dynamic content  most common example is the button tag  the template here is delete hero this  method is called when the user clicks on  the button  so this brings interactivity to your  application  with that we come to the end of the  first section which included the  beginner level questions  moving on let's look at some advanced  level questions  what is the difference between ahead of  time and just in time compilation  now ahead of time compilation converts  your code during the build time  before the browser downloads and runs  the code  in case of just in time compilation this  process is a way of compiling computer  code  to machine code during the execution  phase  aot ensures faster rendering to the  browser  while just in time is basically a  dynamic compilation  in case of ahead of time compiling the  user should include the  hyphen hyphen aot option with the ng  build or ng serve command  and jit compilation is the default  compilation when you run the ng build or  ng  serve cli commands  next up explain the add component  decorator  now here's a simple screenshot of what  that component  decorator encompasses is it is basically  a typescript class  that is used to create components  this genre of class is then decorated  with the add component decorator  the decorators purpose is to accept a  metadata  object that provides relevant  information about  the component now the image above shows  an app component  which is a pure typescript class  decorated with that component decorator  the object  that gets accepted by the decorator  provides properties like  template url selectors style urls  and many more now here the template url  property  points to an html file defining what you  see  on the application moving ahead  what are services in angular angular  services  perform tasks that are used by multiple  components  now these tasks could be data fetching  network connections  or database management among others they  perform  all the operational tasks for the  components and avoid  rewriting of code a service can be  written once and then injected into all  the components that use it  generally components are used to only  display information on the ui  they do not perform any other back-end  tasks  to perform tasks like validating  information  or network connections etc you can make  use of a service  one advantage is that this service can  be injected into multiple components  that make use of the same piece of code  with this you can avoid redundancy  moving on  what are promises and observables now  while both the components deal with  asynchronous events in angular  promises handle one such event at a time  while observables handle a sequence of  events over  some time so to give you a brief  explanation promises emit a single value  at a time  while observables are only executed when  subscribed to them using the subscribe  method now promises also execute  immediately after they're created  and they're not cancelable while  observables help perform operations like  for each  filter retry etc promises  push errors to the child promises and  observables can be unsubscribed to  so that the listener stops receiving  further values  next up what is ng on init and how is it  defined  now again here's a small snippet of code  ng on init is a life cycle hook as we  discussed earlier and there is a  callback method that is run by angular  to indicate that a component has been  created  it takes no parameters and returns a  void type  so i'm sure you can see here in the code  it takes no parameters and returns a  void  next up explain the use of ng4 in a tag  or explain the ng4 directive  now the ng for directive is basically  like a for loop it is used to build  lists and tables and html templates so  in  simple terms this directive is used to  iterate over an array  or an object and create template for  each such element  now in the snippet you can see there is  let items in  item list and then i have string  interpolated the  uh variable item so let item here  creates a local variable that will be  available inside the template  of items indicates that we are iterating  over the items iterable  and the asterisk before ng4 creates a  parent template  next up what are template and reactive  forms so there are two different methods  to create forms  we have the template driven approach and  we have the reactive form approach  so let's have a look at them in case of  template driven approach  the conventional form tag is used to  create forms  angular automatically interprets and  creates a form object  representation for this tag controls can  be added to the form using the  ng model tag multiple controls can be  grouped using the ng control group  module  now a form value can be generated using  the form dot value object  and form data as exported as json values  basic html validations can be used to  validate the form fields  in the case of custom validations  directives can be used  when it comes to reactive forms this  approach  basically revolves around data flows and  propagation of change  now with reactor forms the component  directly manages the data flows between  the form controls and the data models  the active forms are code driven unlike  template driven approach  reactive forms break the traditional  declarative approach  and eliminate the anti-pattern of  updating data via the two-way data  binding method  typically reactive form control creation  is synchronous  and can be unit tested with synchronous  programming techniques  moving on what is bootstrap how is it  added to angular  now bootstrap is a powerful toolkit it  is a collection of basic html css and  javascript tools  for creating and building responsive web  applications  there are two ways to embed bootstrap  libraries  first up is using the bootstrap cdn  which is the content delivery network  now this enables users to load the css  and javascript  files remotely from its servers  the other way is to use angular  bootstrap via npm  now this is used to add bootstrap to  your angular project  by installing it into your project  folder  now you can use commands like npm  install bootstrap  and npm install jquery to install them  for your project  if you wish to learn bootstrap in detail  i highly suggest you check out our video  on angular bootstrap  the tutorial explains how to embed  bootstrap and use it to create and good  looking angular applications  what is eager and lazy loading  eager loading is the default module  loading strategy  now all the feature modules under eager  loading are loaded before your  application even starts  this is typically used for small size  applications since lesser  modules are used all of these modules  are loaded initially which makes  running of these kind of applications  extremely fast  when it comes to lazy loading all the  loading happens dynamically  all feature modules are loaded on demand  it is used for bigger applications where  the modules are not required at the  start of applications  this makes the application faster since  no time is spent on loading unnecessary  modules  next up what type of dom does angular  implement  dom or document object model treats an  xml  or html document as a tree structure  in which each node is an object  representing a part of the document  now angular uses the regular dom this  updates the entire tree structure  of html tags until it reaches the data  that has to be updated  now to ensure that the speed and  performance are not affected  angular implements something called as a  change detection  next up how is dependency injection  achieved in angular now dependencies  are objects or services that a component  needs to perform functions  correct now with the help of dependency  injection  these classes can request dependencies  from external sources  rather than creating them on their own  here i've created a service  called demo service using the command  ngg service demo service  and i've also added a small snippet of  code when  you create that service  now these services can be injected to  your  main component and perform various  functions  next up how does angular routing work  now i'm sure you must have observed that  the url changes  every time you click on your user  interface on an application correct  every time you navigate through the  application or move from one page to  another  the url changes now this means  that the application is being routed or  you're navigating through the  application  so basically routing helps navigate  through a web application  especially in case of single page  applications now as discussed  earlier single-page applications are  loaded just once  so any new content that is being  displayed is just a mere addition it's  not being loaded again  so routing plays a vital role in case of  single page applications  typically it is specified with the help  of the forward slash  and followed by a path that defines a  new content  now i'm just taking the same example  that i took before  this was the example for string  interpolation however you can see that  we have a navigation bar here  with four different options for that is  home about services and login  and for home and login i've created a  path  and added routing to it so when i click  on the home icon  you can see that some content is being  displayed onto the screen  and if you observe you can see that  there is a forward slash  with the path name home here which  indicates that routing has occurred  same with login when i click on it the  path changes  and the login page appears if you wish  to learn  the concept of routing i suggest you  check out a video  the tutorial explains routing in detail  moving on what are form control and form  groups  now a form control is basically a class  that enables  validation for each input field  an instance of this class is created  and these instances help check the  values of the field  and see if they are touched untouched  dirty pristine  valid invalid and so on so for every  field  in the form the data that is being  provided is validated with the help of  these controls  if it is dirty it means that the value  has been changed  if the data provided holds good for a  particular condition  then the control is said to be valid and  so on  with the help of these controls you can  determine if the value provided is  legitimate or not  this can be achieved with the help of  form control  when it comes to form group when the  form group class  represents a group of controls now a  form  can have multiple control groups the  form  group class returns true if all the  controls are valid  and also provides validation errors if  any  next up is how is testing achieved in  angular  now angular uses jasmine to run various  tests  the jasmine framework allows various  functionalities  to write different kinds of test cases  the task runner for these tests is  typically  karma and karma uses a configuration  file  to set the startup reporters and the  testing framework  next question is what is package.json  now npm installs package.json when a new  workspace is created  now this file includes a starter set of  packages  some of which are required by angular  now typically  it's organized into two groups one is  dependencies  these are essential to run your  applications and we have  dev dependencies these are essential to  develop applications  so with that we come to the end of this  session  i hope these interview questions help  you crack your next interview  if you have any doubts or queries let us  know in the comment section below  so thank you so much for being here and  watch out for more videos from us  until then keep learning and stay tuned  to simply learn  hi there if you like this video  subscribe to the simply learn youtube  channel  and click here to watch similar videos  turn it up and get certified  click here
 

